  "Question": "A burger at Ricky C’s weighs \\(120\\) grams, of which \\(30\\) grams are filler. What percent of the burger is not filler?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(60 \\%\\)",
    "B": "\\(65 \\%\\)",
    "C": "\\(70 \\%\\)",
    "D": "\\(75 \\%\\)",
    "E": "\\(90 \\%\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "First subtract the filler from the total mass. The burger contains \\(120-30=90\\) grams that are not filler.\n\nTo find what percent this is, divide that part by the entire burger's mass:\n\\[\n\\frac{90}{120}=0.75=75\\%.\n\\]\nThus \\(75\\%\\) of the burger is not filler, choice \\(D\\).",
